<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Solar on The Miette</title><link>https://lysng.github.io/themiette/tags/solar/</link><description>Recent content in Solar on The Miette</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:15:56 +1000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://lysng.github.io/themiette/tags/solar/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>So, We Moved In</title><link>https://lysng.github.io/themiette/posts/2026-jan-to-oct-build-update/</link><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:15:56 +1000</pubDate><guid>https://lysng.github.io/themiette/posts/2026-jan-to-oct-build-update/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;After years of building, many Bunnings trips and an unreasonable amount of sanding, we finally moved into the Miette in February. It is now October. So, what have we been doing for the last eight months?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Well, apparently the building never really stops.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="centerImage"&gt;&lt;img src="https://lysng.github.io/themiette/images/20261009/20260101_163549.jpg"&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;alt="First two minute noodles in the tiny house"&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;p&gt;First two minute noodles in the tiny house&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure class="centerImage"&gt;&lt;img src="https://lysng.github.io/themiette/images/20261009/20260101_164300.jpg"&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;alt="Close up of our noodles, feels like every new place needs a memorable first meal"&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;p&gt;Close up of our noodles, feels like every new place needs a memorable first meal&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;</description></item><item><title>Oct Build Update</title><link>https://lysng.github.io/themiette/posts/oct-2022-build-update/</link><pubDate>Thu, 10 Nov 2022 11:08:26 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://lysng.github.io/themiette/posts/oct-2022-build-update/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="an-october-build-update"&gt;An October build update&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We got solar! ☀️ ☀️ ☀️&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;&#10; &lt;h6&gt;Table Of Contents&lt;/h6&gt;&#10; &lt;nav id="TableOfContents"&gt;&#10; &lt;ul&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-weve-done"&gt;What we&amp;rsquo;ve done&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#highlights"&gt;Highlights&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#challenges"&gt;Challenges&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#whats-next"&gt;What&amp;rsquo;s next?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/nav&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="what-weve-done"&gt;What we&amp;rsquo;ve done&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;One of our neighbours decided to demolish their house without removing their 10 year old solar system (it was not cost effective for them to re-install). Luckily for us they said that if we could take it down we could have it! Erny clambered onto the roof on a balmy Sunday day to bring the panels down.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>